    "head_branch": "fix/rout-store-reads",
    "head_commit_message": "perf(formation): the rout reads its fleeing columns as typed arrays held for the pass\n\nSince spec 35 moved the fleeing entries into the unit store, the rout read\nand wrote them through `columns.value` and `put`, about 1 us each on the\nnative store, roughly 8,700 calls a tick at 1,024 a side. At 4,096 a side in\nfour squads the rout went from 60.9 to 92.4 ms a tick.\n\nStoreHolds holds the fleeing columns (along, offset, fanned, caught, held_by\nand keys) for the rout's pass: ColumnsHeld copies them out once and serves\nevery reader through `store.columns`, and FleeColumns hands the rout's loops\nand RoutFlight the held copies as typed arrays, read and written in place.\nPacked arrays share their storage in GDScript, so the typed writes are what\nevery other reader in the pass sees; releasing commits them. Outcomes are\nunchanged: two 400-tick battles with routs, crushes and units fleeing home\ngave the same state and events every tick, old against new, on both engines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KKUhViTbS7kfMBSZozDAco",
    "head_sha": "89da83df6d02c4bbd670446d4c3d125366208b86",
